F-1 (Foxy portability): build pcl_ros on Foxy as well as Humble.

The G1's onboard computer runs ROS 2 Foxy (Ubuntu 20.04). Three unrelated
Foxy/Humble differences, none of which change what any filter computes:

1. tf2_geometry_msgs is `.h` on Foxy, `.hpp` from Galactic (transforms.hpp and
   transforms.cpp). Selected with __has_include.

2. pcd_to_pointcloud used two rclcpp 16 (Humble) APIs. declare_parameter<T>(name)
   with no default becomes the with-default form — an unsupplied file_name then
   lands in the `== ""` branch that already logs and throws, so the failure is
   raised by the tool instead of by rclcpp. NodeTopicsInterface::resolve_topic_name()
   falls back to rclcpp::expand_topic_or_service_name(), whose result is only
   ever printed in the adjacent log line.

3. project_inliers declared its mandatory `model_type` by TYPE with no default,
   also rclcpp 16. Foxy's equivalent leaves the parameter PARAMETER_NOT_SET;
   either way the get_parameter() on the next line returns false when no
   override was given, which is the "mandatory parameter missing" path the code
   already handles.

Applies on top of patch 0002 (which touches only filters/filter.cpp).
